Every supported lumi-multitorch variant has a **fixed release**,
whose images no longer trust the root certificate `emSign ECC Root CA - G3`.
It replaces all affected releases of its variant. The newest variant's fixed
release is an official release. For the earlier variants, this hotfix makes
**patched releases**: it patches the latest release of each variant and
publishes the results together as `{{ name }}`. Each patched release is a new
release of its variant, and they all share one build ID. See the notice for
users, [README.md]({{ incident_url }}/README.md), for the affected releases and what to do.

The patched releases are the original releases with only these packages
upgraded to
[versions that no longer trust the root](https://emudhra.we-have-a-problem.com/#patched-bundles):

- `ca-certificates` 20260816ubuntu0.24.04.1, Ubuntu's system CA store, in all
  images,
- `pip` 26.2.2 and `certifi` 2026.10.19 or newer in the images with Python
  packages in `/opt/venv` (torch, full and plus). In the u24r64 torch image,
  which had no `certifi`, `certifi` is added,
- `botocore` 1.43.117 or newer in the images that have it (full and plus), as
  [AWS security bulletin 2026-150-AWS](https://aws.amazon.com/security/security-bulletins/2026-150-aws/)
  advises, with `boto3`, which has to match its version, and in the u24r64
  full image `s3transfer`, which the newer `boto3` needs.

Everything else, including the images' environment and runscript, is as in the
original release.

